# Byte-exact fixtures: git must never translate line endings in them.
#
# "It contains NUL bytes so git treats it as binary" is FALSE in general — git
# scans only the first 8000 bytes for a NUL, and `core.autocrlf` defaults to TRUE
# on GitHub's windows-latest runners. A vault fixture is plain text, so without
# this it WILL have its LF bytes rewritten to CRLF on a Windows checkout, and any
# test asserting on a content hash fails there and nowhere else.
tests/data/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
